  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Shandong Environmental Emergency Response System, through Government of China (P.R.C.)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $346,634 USTDA grant to the Shandong Environmental Protection Bureau supported a feasibility study on the development of an environmental early warning and emergency response command system for Shandong Province. The system would improve environmental real-time data monitoring and analysis; establish an advanced emergency operations and incident response command center; and deploy an effective early warning system for environmental hazards at the provincial, county, and municipal levels. Successful completion of this project would avert environmental disasters in Shandong and serve as a model for the development of environmental response networks across China.</narrative>
  </description>
